0.27065,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MSC Industrial Direct Co., Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the distribution of metalworking and maintenance, repair, and operations (MRO) products and services in the United States, Canada, Mexico, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company offers metalworking and MRO products, including cutting tools, abrasives, machining fluids, measuring instruments, machinery and accessories, tooling components, fasteners, flat stock, raw materials, machinery hand and power tools, safety and janitorial supplies, plumbing supplies, materials handling products, power transmission components and electrical supplies, as well as stock-keeping units. It serves individual machine shops, companies, and manufacturers, as well as federal agencies, state governments, and public sector healthcare providers. The company was founded in 1941 and is headquartered in Melville, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Martina  McIsaac | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $586K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["MSC Industrial Direct Company,  is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.3B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow 